      "claim": "Molsidomine, a morpholine-containing drug, had absolute bioavailability of 44 ± 15% after oral dosing, well above the 20% threshold and supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C35"],
      "claim": "Isoniazid, a small polar hydrazide, had 91.4% oral bioavailability in patients, supporting high F for small polar amide-like drugs.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C03"],
      "claim": "Imatinib, a larger oral drug, had 98% absolute bioavailability, supporting high F.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All retrieved high-transfer experimental analogues show absolute oral bioavailability well above 20% (44–100%), with direct IV comparisons in humans. No affirmative evidence of low bioavailability was found, so the query is predicted high.",
